{
	quest.06A06D32610AF104.quest_desc: [
		"Pressing &eA&r while hovering over an item will add the item to your Favorites. You can find the list of your Favorites on the left side of your inventory."
		""
		"If you press &eA&r while hovering over an item inside of the output a recipe menu, it'll add the recipe to the Favorites instead, allowing you to quick access the recipe without having to shift through the different pages. This will also allow you to autofill the items into the appropriate slots if you have the correct container open."
	]
	quest.0FCA538AF088692D.quest_desc: [
		"If you ever heard of veinminer, then you know what Ultimine is."
		""
		"Ultimine allows you to break multiple blocks at once, as if you broke every block yourself. Check your keybinds for a \"FTB Ultimine\" key. When holding that keybind while aiming at a block will outline the blocks that will be broken. If you break the block you're looking at, every block that was outlined will go with it!"
		""
		"You can even select different shapes by holding the keybind, Shift and then scrolling with your mouse wheel. &8(If you don't have a mouse wheel, you can also set keybinds to move between shapes.)&r There's a bunch of different shapes that will come in handy in different situations, such as the Small Square, that'll mine a 3x3 area!"
	]
	quest.10582A9E064440AB.quest_desc: [
		"You have probably noticed the menu on the right side of your inventory. That's &#EB7BFCE&#7BFCA2M&#7BEBFCI&r!"
		""
		"It's a great tool for modded Minecraft, as it allows you to look up any item and recipe found in the modpack. By default, it only shows items if you type anything in the search bar or if you press the &7Show Recipes&r button."
		""
		"Left clicking an item in &#EB7BFCE&#7BFCA2M&#7BEBFCI&r or pressing &eR&r while hovering over an item in an inventory will show you every way you can craft said item. Right clicking or pressing &eU&r will show you what the item can be used in!"
		"&8This assumes you have default keybinds.&r"
		""
		"If you're inside of a container, such as a Crafting Table, and are looking at a recipe, you can press the Fill Recipe"
		"{image:ftbquests:textures/emi/fill_recipe.png width:16 height:16 align:center}"
		"button and the items will be moved from your inventory to the correct slots, provided you have the items in your inventory."
	]
	quest.10582A9E064440AB.title: "&#EB7BFCE&#7BFCA2M&#7BEBFCI&r"
	quest.10AFB3C1293D31BF.quest_desc: [
		"You might be wondering what &#EB7BFCE&#7BFCA2M&#7BEBFCI&r stands for. JEI stands for Just Enough Items and REI for Roughly Enough Items."
		""
		"So what the hell does &#EB7BFCE&#7BFCA2M&#7BEBFCI&r mean? Well, this quest will reveal it!"
		""
		"It stands for"
		"&#EB7BFCEmi &#7BFCA2Memy &#7BEBFCImi&r"
		"no wait that's not right, it stands for"
		"&#EB7BFCExhaustively &#7BFCA2Many &#7BEBFCItems&r"
		"no that's not correct either... it's"
		"&#EB7BFCEven &#7BFCA2More &#7BEBFCItems&r"
		"that's not correct either... hmm.. it's actually"
		"&#EB7BFCEmi's &#7BFCA2Magic &#7BEBFCInventory&r"
		"uuuh... not that one either..."
		""
		"&#EB7BFCI&#7BFCA2D&#7BEBFCK&r"
	]
	quest.22D0F35B8FABC316.quest_desc: [
		"The Recipe Tree is what truly sets &#EB7BFCE&#7BFCA2M&#7BEBFCI&r apart from other recipe viewer mods, such as JEI or REI. It allows you to get a tree of every step you have to take to craft a specific item."
		""
		"While looking at a recipe of any item, you can press the View Recipe Tree"
		"{image:ftbquests:textures/emi/view_recipe_tree.png width:16 height:16 align:center}"
		"button to open the item's Recipe Tree."
		""
		"Depending on what item you chose, you might have to expand the tree further by clicking on an item and then pressing the Set as default recipe"
		"{image:ftbquests:textures/emi/default_recipe.png width:16 height:16 align:center}"
		"button on the correct recipe to continue the tree."
		""
		"Eventually, you end up with a full Recipe Tree, showing you every step, every item you need and even items that will be leftover when you're done crafting."
		""
		"You can adjust the amount you want to craft by scrolling on top of the x1."
		""
		"Pressing the icon next to the Total Cost"
		"{image:ftbquests:textures/emi/search.png width:16 height:16 align:center}"
		"will toggle Crafting mode. This will add every item needed to your &eFavorites&r and automatically remove them whenever you get certain items in your inventory, until you eventually have the end result."
	]
	quest.27C1FA13E930237A.quest_desc: [
		"FTB mods are important parts of most modpacks. They provide quests, teams and other useful features."
		""
		"You can find most buttons for FTB mods on the top left corner of your inventory."
	]
	quest.33B98B6A1C3A6F3F.quest_desc: [
		"Here's some starter gear to get you started in the modpack."
		""
		"Quests are currently work in progress, so stay tuned for future updates!"
	]
	quest.33B98B6A1C3A6F3F.title: "Welcome to Horizon!"
	quest.34FEA75350398792.quest_desc: [
		"Pressing the icon on the right menu"
		"{image:ftbquests:textures/emi/search.png width:16 height:16 align:center}"
		"will switch the menu to only show Craftables. This means, it'll show whatever you can currently craft with the items in your inventory in whatever container you have currently open."
		""
		"Pressing the icon"
		"{image:ftbquests:textures/emi/craftables.png width:16 height:16 align:center}"
		"will switch it back to Index mode, showing every item."
	]
	quest.43F37CCB2BD76D6E.quest_desc: [
		"On the top left of your inventory, you will find the Claim Manager. Clicking on it will open a small map of your current area. You can now click through different chunks to claim them. Right clicking will unclaim them."
		""
		"When a chunk is claimed, it'll protect from most destructive events, such as creeper explosions. In multiplayer, claims will prevent other players from being able to destroy any blocks and even interacting with certain blocks, such as chests."
		""
		"If you want to give certain players to interact inside of your claims, you will have to either ally them or invite them to your team. Check the Teams quest for more information."
	]
	quest.517647D70EEA8897.quest_desc: [
		"The Teams button can be found on the top left of your inventory. Clicking it will open a new menu, where you can create a brand new team."
		""
		"Teams essentially allow you to trust players and/or even share quest progress."
		""
		"After creating a team, you will be able to ally players by clicking the &oManage Allies&r button."
		"{image:ftblibrary:icons/friends width:16 height:16 align:center}"
		"You can then add a player to the list, provided their are online. Allied players will now be able to interact with anything inside of your claims."
		""
		"You also will be able to directly invite players to your team by pressing the &oInvite Player(s)&r button."
		"{image:ftblibrary:icons/add width:16 height:16 align:center}"
		"Clicking a player will invite them to your team. Unlike the ally system, players will need to accept the invite first. A player can only be in one team at a time. Players in a team will share quest progress and claims with each other."
	]
	quest.5AF6D83D13000C23.quest_desc: [
		"Congratulations! You managed to complete a &zHidden Quest&r!"
		""
		"&zHidden Quests&r are quests that aren't visible until you complete them. They're easter eggs found within the pack, that can range between silly jokes to difficult challenges. They are indicated by their &zrainbow names&r."
	]
	quest.5AF6D83D13000C23.title: "&zHidden Quests&r"
	quest.676FD6E3678954FA.quest_desc: [
		"Pressing the trash can icon at the top left of your inventory will open a new menu."
		"Any item moved inside of the container will be deleted when closed."
		""
		"&4<fade f=2>Be careful what you put in there, as there's no way to recover the items!</fade>&r"
	]
	quest.7B76175335DBA6F6.quest_desc: [
		"The search bar searches for items that have whatever you input in its name or tooltip. There's also some useful prefixes you can use that'll make the search bar even more powerful."
		""
		"Appending an &#5454FC@&r will make it search by mod names instead. So, &#5454FC@cobblemon&r will show you everything added by Cobblemon (and any other mod that has Cobblemon in its name)."
		""
		"Putting &#54FC54\\#&r in front will search it by tags instead. Searching &#54FC54\\#poke_balls&r, for example, will show you every item inside of the poke_balls tag!"
		""
		"Using &#FC5454-&r will instead hide whatever you're \"searching\" for. &#FC5454-&rred will hide everything that has \"red\" in its name or tooltip. This can be combined with other prefixes. &#FC5454-&#5454FC@create&r will hide everything related to the Create mod."
		""
		"If you don't want to always search for whatever is in tooltips, you can disable it in &#EB7BFCE&#7BFCA2M&#7BEBFCI&r's settings and then use &#FCFC54$&r to search for tooltips instead."
		""
		"Searches are normally ANDs, so searching \"red blue\" will search for items that have both \"red\" and \"blue\" in their name (or tooltip). You can use &5|&r to make it an OR search instead. This means searching \"red | blue\" will search for items that either have \"red\" or \"blue\" in their name."
		""
		"You can, of course, combine everything above to make your ultimate specific search. For example, \"&#5454FC@minecraft&r &#54FC54\\#logs&r | ingot &#FC5454-&rtemplate\" will search for items that are Minecraft and in the logs tag or for any item that has ingot in its name or tooltip ignoring Smithing Templates."
	]
	task.03E5BDC6B53A8CED.title: "EMI"
